        "sourceCitations": [
          {
            "path": "The Cosmology of Decennium Descent.docx",
            "evidenceKind": "verbatim-source-paragraph",
            "part": "word/document.xml",
            "paragraphIndexZeroBased": 270,
            "excerpt": "Crystalfall archivists have released the Spiral Map in Still Time, a cosmograph that freezes momentary relations among planes for study. In abstract art form the map resembles a nautilus cross section. Each chamber corresponds to one realm."
          },
          {
            "path": "The Cosmology of Decennium Descent.docx",
            "evidenceKind": "verbatim-source-paragraph",
            "part": "word/document.xml",
            "paragraphIndexZeroBased": 271,
            "excerpt": "The Bastion of Flame occupies the first coil, indicated by ruby ink that fades toward amber at its outer edge, symbolizing disciplined passion that may chill into temperance."
          },
          {
            "path": "The Cosmology of Decennium Descent.docx",
            "evidenceKind": "verbatim-source-paragraph",
            "part": "word/document.xml",
            "paragraphIndexZeroBased": 272,
            "excerpt": "The Veiled Expanse appears as charcoal wash, darkest near the incarceration seal, lightening toward the Spiral path, showing secrecy that surrenders when engaged with honest motion."
          },
          {
            "path": "The Cosmology of Decennium Descent.docx",
            "evidenceKind": "verbatim-source-paragraph",
            "part": "word/document.xml",
            "paragraphIndexZeroBased": 273,
            "excerpt": "The Radiant Currents swirl in layered pearl, emphasizing fluid law. Viewers see faint afterimages shift as they step, teaching that dream responds to perspective."
          },
          {
            "path": "The Cosmology of Decennium Descent.docx",
            "evidenceKind": "verbatim-source-paragraph",
            "part": "word/document.xml",
            "paragraphIndexZeroBased": 274,
            "excerpt": "The Boundless Void fills a thin white crescent marked by pinprick glints, representing questions that puncture complacency."
          },
          {
            "path": "The Cosmology of Decennium Descent.docx",
            "evidenceKind": "verbatim-source-paragraph",
            "part": "word/document.xml",
            "paragraphIndexZeroBased": 275,
            "excerpt": "The Citadel of Many Echoes is a small diamond placed between coils two and three, signifying its role as resonance archive bridging shadow and dream. The Nine Hells lie beneath the nautilus shell in a mirrored spiral that turns the opposite direction, a deliberate choice to illustrate lawful ambition forever circling chaos in counter rotation. The Abyss sits beyond that mirror, rendered by blank canvas rather than pigment, a visual silence."
          },
          {
            "path": "The Cosmology of Decennium Descent.docx",
            "evidenceKind": "verbatim-source-paragraph",
            "part": "word/document.xml",
            "paragraphIndexZeroBased": 276,
            "excerpt": "Game masters can present the map during session zero. When players choose a home plane they place a token on the corresponding coil. Each long rest taken away from that coil grants either Inspiration or Disquiet, determined by whether the character acts in accordance with their home plane principle that day."
          },
          {
            "path": "books/player/Decennium_Descent_Player_Rulebook_v6.docx",
            "evidenceKind": "verbatim-source-paragraph",
            "part": "word/document.xml",
            "paragraphIndexZeroBased": 9977,
            "excerpt": "The beliefs recorded in this appendix are mortal theology, not objective cosmic history. Priests, scholars, and cults across Aethel have spent millennia reasoning about forces they cannot fully perceive. What follows is what the faithful believe: a creation myth, a pantheon of worshiped faces, and a diagram of the planes — sincerely held, widely taught, and useful for understanding how ordinary people in Aethel think about the divine. Your character may treat this as literal truth. Deeper mysteries of the Spiral and the Crucible may surface only through play; even then, the wider world does not rewrite its temples overnight. Scholars may also speak of the First Choir — seven named virtues (Korvelan, Vaerilune, Delvaran, Shaelara, Xalarex, Thalirion, and Virellian) — as part of the wider Spiral story. That knowledge is not secret, but it is not tavern talk either."
          },
          {
            "path": "DescentReviewChanges/ReviewBible/docs/canon/PLAYER_DIRECTOR_BOUNDARY.md",
            "evidenceKind": "verbatim-markdown-line",
            "lineOneBased": 15,
